# Cloud AI Orchestration Platform

Multi-cloud **workflow orchestration platform** for AI data pipelines — built for roles requiring **AWS/Azure**, **distributed systems**, **PostgreSQL**, **retries/idempotency**, and **LLM integration with human oversight**.

[![Deploy to Render](https://render.com/images/deploy-to-render-button.svg)](https://render.com/deploy?repo=https://github.com/Ananyanagaraj11/ananya-cloud-ai-orchestration-platform)

## Live demos

| Service | URL |
|---------|-----|
| API (Swagger) | https://ananya-cloud-ai-orchestration-platform.onrender.com/docs |
| Dashboard | https://ananya-cloud-orchestration-dashboard.onrender.com |

## Why this project exists

Top companies (AI marketplaces, enterprise banks, applied AI teams) need engineers who can build **long-running, reliable workflows** that combine **models + humans + backend infrastructure**. This repo demonstrates that stack.

## Architecture

```
Client → FastAPI → Workflow Engine → Steps (ingest, validate, LLM, HITL, export)
                         ↓
              PostgreSQL/SQLite state · Redis queue · Audit log
                         ↓
              Prometheus metrics · OpenTelemetry-ready · AWS/Azure deploy docs
```

## Features

- **Workflow orchestration**: multi-step pipelines with state persistence
- **Idempotency keys** — duplicate requests return the same run
- **Retries** via tenacity on step execution
- **Human-in-the-loop** approval gate before export
- **Audit trail** per workflow run
- **Prometheus** `/metrics` endpoint
- **AWS + Azure** deployment guides (ECS/EKS, AKS, Container Apps)
- **Docker Compose** local stack (API + PostgreSQL + Redis)

## Stack

Python · FastAPI · SQLAlchemy · PostgreSQL · Redis · Prometheus · Streamlit · Docker · GitHub Actions

## Quick start

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
uvicorn src.api.main:app --reload --port 8040
```

## API

```bash
curl http://localhost:8040/health
curl -X POST http://localhost:8040/workflows -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"idempotency_key\":\"demo-1\"}"
```

## Cloud deployment

See `docs/AWS-DEPLOY.md` and `docs/AZURE-DEPLOY.md` for ECS/EKS and AKS/Container Apps patterns.

## Testing

```bash
pytest tests -q
ruff check src tests
```

